# Navigable menus own the wheel

Law: **P0.10** in `docs/keymap/contracts/PATTERNS.md`. The owner is
`atlas_shell::menu_wheel`.

Any open list, dropdown, scrolling popup, or menu takes wheel and pinch input
while the pointer is over it. The canvas underneath never zooms or pans.

- A menu you paint yourself calls `menu_wheel::claim(ctx, rect)` every pass
  it is open. `selection_tools::capsule_menu` already does this. egui combo
  boxes are detected without a claim.
- Every canvas camera (Slate board, File Atlas, portal cameras) checks
  `menu_wheel::wheel_owned(ctx)` before wheel zoom, Shift+wheel pan, or pinch.
- Do not add a per-menu "pointer over my popup" flag to one canvas. That was
  the recurring bug.

```rust
// BAD - the typeface list scrolled and the board zoomed under it
if resp.hovered() || palette_wheel { zoom(scroll) }

// GOOD
if (resp.hovered() || palette_wheel) && !atlas_shell::menu_wheel::wheel_owned(ctx) {
    zoom(scroll)
}
```
